I've been busily working on improving the chapter, incorporating all  
the feedback so far. I tested the original chapter against someone, M,  
who had never seen constructed language, and is monolingual in English  
(with a smattering of Spanish).

M had interpreted {zo'e} as being the preposition "in". While not  
correct, it is also logical given the input. I realized that errors of  
interpretation can and will occur during language acquisition, and  
this is just a natural part of the process, and hopefully future input  
would correct the problem. The last thing I want to do is overwhelm  
the reader by presenting the CLL in footnotes :)

M did interpret everything else correctly :)

la rab,rt.


